{"qid":"Q175276","names":["Kingdom of León"],"title":"Kingdom of León","endonym":{"native":"Reinu de Llión","lang":"ast"},"capsule":"The Kingdom of León emerged in 910 when King García I moved the Asturian court south to León, reflecting the reconquest of the Duero valley from Moorish control. Alfonso V (r. 999–1028) repopulated and legally reorganized León after a devastating Andalusian raid in 988, issuing the Fueros of León in 1017, the earliest surviving municipal charter in Iberian history. The kingdom was repeatedly united with and separated from Castile; the definitive union occurred under Fernando III, who inherited León in 1230 on the death of his father Alfonso IX, merging the two crowns permanently and launching the major reconquest campaigns that took Córdoba (1236) and Seville (1248).","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The Kingdom of León's territory is broadly attested through chronicles and legal documents, but frontier zones with Castile, Navarre, and al-Andalus shifted frequently and are only approximately reconstructed for any given decade.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Kingdom of León","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Le%C3%B3n"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Alfonso V of León","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfonso_V_of_Le%C3%B3n"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Fernando III of Castile","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferdinand_III_of_Castile"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Kingdom of León","rulers":[{"qid":"Q333699","name":"García I of León","start":910,"end":914,"image":"García I, rey de León.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki